# Nivo78 Rule Projection — 12-release-supply-chain

**Binding status:** This file is a maintained enforcement projection of the canonical Nivo78 Product Standard.
**Source:** `reference/NIVO78_APP_STANDARD.txt`
**Authority:** The canonical standard and rule-ID catalog control if this projection and the source ever differ.

## Agent instructions
- Apply this rule whenever the work described by the rule is relevant.
- Treat every requirement below as binding unless the canonical standard marks it as `[QA]`/conditional or an approved override applies.
- Preserve and mention canonical `APP-*`, `WEB-*`, `MARKETING-*`, and other rule IDs when reporting compliance or exceptions.
- Do not weaken a requirement merely because it is inconvenient to implement.
- If a requirement cannot be met, stop before shipping and use the standard override process.

---

RELEASE ENGINEERING AND SUPPLY CHAIN (APP-RELEASE-\*,
APP-DEPENDENCY-\*, APP-SUPPLY-CHAIN-\*)

\================================================================================



APP-RELEASE-DEFINITION-OF-DONE [GATE]

\- A product is release-ready only when required
builds, static checks, automated tests, security checks,

  accessibility
checks, documentation, migration tests, and release verification have passed.



APP-RELEASE-VERSION-CONSISTENCY [GATE]

\- Application version, package/build version,
displayed version, release metadata, and required

  documentation
must be synchronized before release.



APP-RELEASE-SIGNING [GATE]

\- Production signing keys must be protected from
ordinary development use.

\- Release artifacts must be signed using the
authorized production signing process.



APP-RELEASE-DEBUG-CLEAN [GATE]

\- Production artifacts must be verified to exclude
debug-only code, test data, test credentials,

  development
endpoints, and development-only configuration.



APP-DEPENDENCY-INVENTORY [QA]

\- Each product must maintain an inventory of direct
and material transitive dependencies used in the

  shipped
product.



APP-DEPENDENCY-VULNERABILITY [GATE]

\- Dependencies must be checked for known material
security vulnerabilities before release.

\- Release-blocking vulnerabilities require remediation
or a documented approved exception.



APP-DEPENDENCY-LICENSE [GATE]

\- Dependencies must have license terms reviewed for
compatibility with the product's distribution

  and commercial
use.



APP-SUPPLY-CHAIN-SOURCE [QA]

\- Dependencies and build tools should come from
trusted, documented sources.

\- Unnecessary or unmaintained dependencies should not
be introduced.



APP-RELEASE-ARTIFACT-INTEGRITY [GATE]

\- The artifact submitted for distribution must be the
same verified artifact produced by the release

  process; do
not rebuild an unverified variant after final QA.



APP-RELEASE-PUBLISH-SPINE [GATE]

\- Every Nivo78 product repository MUST be registered in the
family publish catalog (N78-Ops/tools/maintain/N78-PublishCatalog.ps1)
before its first store or Play upload.

\- New utilities stamped from N78-Kit MUST receive publish-spine
registration (catalog row + N78-{Name}-Publish.bat + Desktop Apps twin)
in the same stamp pass as cleanscript and updocs.

\- Store products MUST NOT ship first upload until the catalog lists a
real ArtifactKind (Msix, MsixApa, PlayAab, AndroidAab) plus version and
pack metadata. ArtifactKind None only while packaging is being wired.

\- One spine only: N78-Ops/tools/maintain/run-publish.ps1. See
reference/NIVO78_PUBLISH_SPINE.txt.

